{
  "title": "Rhabdomyosarcoma",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8059/rhabdomyosarcoma",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 22 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Rhabdomyosarcomas are malignant tumors of the primitive mesenchyme that come in 4 sub-types: embryonal, alveolar, botryoid, and pleomorphic.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The embryonal and botryoid sub-types most commonly present in young children, the alveolar sub-type most commonly occurs in young adults, and the pleomorphic sub-type most commonly occurs in older patients.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with a biopsy. Immunostains are positive for desmin, myosin and vimentin.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually wide surgical excision with chemotherapy or radiation depending on the sub-type.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Rhabdomyosarcoma is the **most common sarcoma in children**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Four sub-types of rhabdomyosarcoma",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Embryonal**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "occurs in infants and young children",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Alveolar**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "occurs in adolescents and young adults",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Botryoid**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "occurs in infants and young children, typically in the vagina",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "aka Sarcoma botryoides or \"bunch of grapes\"",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Pleomorphic**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "tends to occur in older patients 40-70yrs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "alveolar rhabdomyosarcoma has a common t(2;13) translocation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "forms Pax3-FKHR fusion protein",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "associated with a high risk metastatic disease",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Metastasis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**nodal metastasis** are known to occur with rhabdomyosarcoma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "consider sentinel lymph node biopsy as part of treatment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**bone marrow biopsy** is required for staging",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "bone marrow metastases have been shown to portend a worse prognosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Symptoms",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Presentation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**rapidly growing painless mass**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "most lesions occur in the head/neck, genitourinary system, or retroperitoneum",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "CT of the chest is required for staging of disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "non-diagnostic but crucial for treatment planning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "rhabdomyosarcoma images appear like many other soft tissue sarcomas",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**dark on T1, bright on T2**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Histology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Characteristic histology includes",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Embryonal**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "small round blue cell tumor",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8059/images/51d_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "skeletal muscle-like cross-striations can occur",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "based on the stage of neoplastic cell development",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Alveolar**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "poorly differentiated round cells with multinucleated giant cells",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cellular aggregates are surrounded by dense fibrous septae",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8059/images/51c_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Pleomorphic**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "multiple cell types present",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "difficult to differentiate from other pleomorphic sarcomas",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Immunohistochemistry",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "MyoD1 positive",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "myoglobin positive",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "myosin positive",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "desmin positive",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "vimentin positive",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
